          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            On the one hand, a map into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %em classifies
            some kind of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+morphism"} classifying morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
          %p
            On the other hand, the more refined concept of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            is such that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            into it characterize the object itself. Hence it makes sense to say that such maps into moduli stacks do not just classify, but
            %strong modulate
            the given object.
          %p
            Indeed, that is the idea that originally gave rise to the name
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli"} moduli
            = succeed "Because," do
              %br/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{F}
            of a certain kind of objects is such that morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi χ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\chi}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{F}
            into it determine a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  X
                  }
          %p
            of
            = succeed "-like" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{F}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
