          %h3#metric_structure Metric structure
          %p
            To see that the difference really matters, consider the map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B O(n) \longrightarrow B GL(n)
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            and
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
            these are different, their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            are the same. Accordingly the above map is in fact a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            and accordingly for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            any
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            is classified by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \tau_\Sigma \colon \Sigma \longrightarrow B GL(n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \hat \tau_\Sigma
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi ι
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi τ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                  %mi Σ
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi ι
                              %msub
                                %mi τ
                                %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; B O(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\iota \hat \tau_\Sigma}} \nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma &amp;\stackrel{\iota \tau_\Sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B GL(n)
                  }
          %p
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+space"} contractible
          %p However, there is an important difference which the modulating morphisms do see. Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}O(n) \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}GL(n)
          %p
            for the corresponding morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            (see at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            for more on this). Then a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            of the modulating map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_\Sigma \colon \Sigma \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            to one that modulates an actual orthogonal bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi e
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi τ
                                %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} O(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{e}} \nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma &amp;\stackrel{\tau_\Sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(n)
                  }
          %p
            is genuine data: this is a choice of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %h3#structure_for_maximal_compact_subgroup_inclusions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            \-Structure for maximal compact subgroup inclusions
          %p
            An analogous situation is obtained for any inclusion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
            into a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            and the corresponding notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structure"} twisted differential c-structure
            for a list of further examples
          %h2#references References
          %p The terminology “modulating” in the context of “moduli stacks” would seem to be inevitable but is not used much in practice. One place where it is used consistently is
          %ul
            %li#BenZvi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
              ,
              %em Moduli Spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/benzvi/math/pcm0178.pdf"}> pdf
              )
